IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eca-nouns`
IMPORT `eca-schedules`
IMPORT `eca-part1-preliminary`
IMPORT `eca-part3-proceedings`

-- Tests of Part 3, Division 3 (ss 18 to 22).  Every expected value was decided from the text before the run and is written beside its assertion.
-- Amounts are arbitrary test values: the Act fixes none of them.

§ `Tests -- s 18`

#ASSERT `s 18(1) the proceedings before the tribunal are conducted in private` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 18(1) the proceedings before the tribunal are conducted in private` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 18(2)(a) the tribunal may allow individuals to assist in resolving the claim amicably` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 18(2)(a) the tribunal may allow individuals to assist in resolving the claim amicably` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 18(2)(a) the tribunal may allow individuals to assist in resolving the claim amicably` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 18(2)(b) the tribunal may allow the individual to sit with the tribunal and act as an assessor` (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 18(2)(b) the tribunal may allow the individual to sit with the tribunal and act as an assessor` (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 18(2)(b) the tribunal may allow the individual to sit with the tribunal and act as an assessor` NOTHING TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 18(3) the tribunal may permit the officer to participate in the proceedings` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 18(3) the tribunal may permit the officer to participate in the proceedings` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 18(3) the tribunal may permit the officer to participate in the proceedings` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 18(4) the tribunal may permit the individual to observe the hearing of the claim` (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE  -- (a) or (b)
#ASSERT `s 18(4) the tribunal may permit the individual to observe the hearing of the claim` (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE  -- (c)
#ASSERT `s 18(4) the tribunal may permit the individual to observe the hearing of the claim` NOTHING TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 18(4) the tribunal may permit the individual to observe the hearing of the claim` (JUST FALSE) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 18(4) the tribunal may permit the individual to observe the hearing of the claim` NOTHING FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 18(6) subsection (1) does not prevent the tribunal from hearing the claims together` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 18(6) subsection (1) does not prevent the tribunal from hearing the claims together` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 18(6) subsection (1) does not prevent the tribunal from hearing the claims together` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 18(6) subsection (1) does not prevent the tribunal from hearing the claims together` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- s 19`

#ASSERT `s 19(5) the entity is a body corporate` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 19(5) the entity is a body corporate` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 19(5) the person is an officer of the body corporate` `Director` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 19(5) the person is an officer of the body corporate` `Partner` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 19(5) the person is an officer of the body corporate` `Member of the committee of management` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 19(5) the person is an officer of the body corporate` `Chief executive` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 19(5) the person is an officer of the body corporate` `Manager` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 19(5) the person is an officer of the body corporate` `Secretary` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 19(5) the person is an officer of the body corporate` `Another position` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 19(5) the person is an officer of the body corporate` `Another position` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

#ASSERT `s 19(1) to (3) the party may be represented before the tribunal by the representative` `The Government` `A public officer` NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE  -- (2)(a)
#ASSERT `s 19(1) to (3) the party may be represented before the tribunal by the representative` `The Government` `A full-time employee of the party` NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 19(1) to (3) the party may be represented before the tribunal by the representative` `A body corporate` `An officer of the body corporate` NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE  -- (2)(b)
#ASSERT `s 19(1) to (3) the party may be represented before the tribunal by the representative` `A body corporate` `A full-time employee of the party` NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE  -- (2)(b)
#ASSERT `s 19(1) to (3) the party may be represented before the tribunal by the representative` `A partnership` `A partner of the partnership` NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE  -- (2)(c)
#ASSERT `s 19(1) to (3) the party may be represented before the tribunal by the representative` `A partnership` `A full-time employee of the party` NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE  -- (2)(c)
#ASSERT `s 19(1) to (3) the party may be represented before the tribunal by the representative` `An unincorporated association` `A member of the governing body of the unincorporated association` NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE  -- (2)(d)
#ASSERT `s 19(1) to (3) the party may be represented before the tribunal by the representative` `An unincorporated association` `A full-time employee of the party` NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE  -- (2)(d)
#ASSERT `s 19(1) to (3) the party may be represented before the tribunal by the representative` `A body corporate` `Another individual prescribed by regulations` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE  -- (2)(e)
#ASSERT `s 19(1) to (3) the party may be represented before the tribunal by the representative` `An individual` `Another individual prescribed by regulations` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE  -- (3)
#ASSERT `s 19(1) to (3) the party may be represented before the tribunal by the representative` `An individual` `Another individual prescribed by regulations` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 19(1) to (3) the party may be represented before the tribunal by the representative` `An individual` `Another individual prescribed by regulations` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 19(1) to (3) the party may be represented before the tribunal by the representative` `An individual` `An advocate and solicitor` NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- (1)(b)
#ASSERT `s 19(1) to (3) the party may be represented before the tribunal by the representative` `A body corporate` `An advocate and solicitor` NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 19(1) to (3) the party may be represented before the tribunal by the representative` `An individual` `An agent, whether paid or otherwise` NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- (1)(c)
#ASSERT `s 19(1) to (3) the party may be represented before the tribunal by the representative` `An individual` `A full-time employee of the party` NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 19(1) to (3) the party may be represented before the tribunal by the representative` `An individual` `Anyone else` NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- (1)(a)

-- s 19(1)(b), (c) as regulative rules.  Trace 1: advocate and solicitor -> BREACH.  Trace 2: agent -> BREACH.  Trace 3: a different act leaves the agent prohibition standing.
#TRACE `s 19(1)(b) the party's prohibition on representation by an advocate and solicitor` `A party` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `A party` DOES `be represented by an advocate and solicitor` AT 5
#TRACE `s 19(1)(c) the party's prohibition on representation by an agent` `A party` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `A party` DOES `be represented by an agent` AT 5
#TRACE `s 19(1)(c) the party's prohibition on representation by an agent` `A party` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `A party` DOES `be represented by an advocate and solicitor` AT 5

§ `Tests -- s 20`

#ASSERT `s 20(1) the proceedings before the tribunal are to be conducted in an informal manner` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 20(1) the proceedings before the tribunal are to be conducted in an informal manner` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 20(2)(a) the tribunal is to identify the relevant issues in the claim` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 20(2)(a) the tribunal is to identify the relevant issues in the claim` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 20(2)(b) the tribunal is to ensure that the relevant evidence is adduced by the parties` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 20(2)(b) the tribunal is to ensure that the relevant evidence is adduced by the parties` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 20(3) the tribunal may direct a party to appear before it` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 20(3) the tribunal may direct a party to appear before it` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 20(4) the tribunal may summon the person` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 20(4) the tribunal may summon the person` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 20(5) the tribunal may inquire into the matter` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 20(5) the tribunal may inquire into the matter` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 20(6) the tribunal may take into account the tripartite guidelines on re-employment` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 20(6) the tribunal may take into account the tripartite guidelines on re-employment` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 20(7)(a) the tribunal is to have regard to the tripartite guidelines on wrongful dismissal` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 20(7)(a) the tribunal is to have regard to the tripartite guidelines on wrongful dismissal` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 20(7)(b) the tribunal is to calculate the compensation in accordance with the regulations made under section 34(1)` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 20(7)(b) the tribunal is to calculate the compensation in accordance with the regulations made under section 34(1)` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- no compensation claimed
#ASSERT `s 20(7)(b) the tribunal is to calculate the compensation in accordance with the regulations made under section 34(1)` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 20(8) the tribunal may hear the claim and make its decision in the absence of the party` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 20(8) the tribunal may hear the claim and make its decision in the absence of the party` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Tests -- s 21`

#ASSERT `s 21(1)(a) the tribunal is not bound by the rules of evidence` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 21(1)(b) the tribunal may inform itself on any matter in any manner it thinks fit` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 21(2) the tribunal may draw any inference it thinks fit from the party's failure` (`A Fourth Schedule obligation` `Item 1: an employer's obligations under EA 1968 s 95, 95A and 96`) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 21(2) the tribunal may draw any inference it thinks fit from the party's failure` (`A Fourth Schedule obligation` `Item 2: an employer's obligations under para 6A of Part IV of the Fourth Schedule to the Employment of Foreign Manpower (Work Passes) Regulations 2012`) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 21(2) the tribunal may draw any inference it thinks fit from the party's failure` (`A Fourth Schedule obligation` `Item 3: an employer's obligations under para 5 of Part II of the Fifth Schedule to the Employment of Foreign Manpower (Work Passes) Regulations 2012`) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 21(2) the tribunal may draw any inference it thinks fit from the party's failure` (`A Fourth Schedule obligation` `Item 1: an employer's obligations under EA 1968 s 95, 95A and 96`) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING  -- the party complied
#ASSERT `s 21(2) the tribunal may draw any inference it thinks fit from the party's failure` `Some other obligation` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 21(2) the inference may include that unavailable evidence would, if produced, have been unfavourable to the party` (`A Fourth Schedule obligation` `Item 1: an employer's obligations under EA 1968 s 95, 95A and 96`) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 21(2) the inference may include that unavailable evidence would, if produced, have been unfavourable to the party` `Some other obligation` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 21(3) the evidence need not be given on oath or affirmation` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 21(3) the evidence need not be given on oath or affirmation` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 21(4)(a) the tribunal may require evidence to be given on oath or affirmation` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 21(4)(b) the tribunal may administer an oath or affirmation for that purpose` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 21(5) the tribunal may seek other evidence and make other investigations and inquiries on its own initiative` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 21(6) the evidence and information must be disclosed to every party to the proceedings` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 21(6) the evidence and information must be disclosed to every party to the proceedings` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 21(7) the tribunal may require written evidence to be verified by statutory declaration` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 21(8) the tribunal need not keep a record of the evidence given` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 21(8)(a) the tribunal must make a summary of the facts and issues in dispute` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 21(8)(a) the tribunal must make a summary of the facts and issues in dispute` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 21(8)(b) the tribunal must make notes of the proceedings` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 21(8)(b) the tribunal must make notes of the proceedings` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 21(6) and (8) as regulative rules.  Trace 4: disclosure done -> FULFILLED.  Trace 5: nothing done -> the duty stands.  Trace 6: summary made -> FULFILLED.  Trace 7: notes made -> FULFILLED.
#TRACE `s 21(6) the tribunal's duty to disclose the evidence it obtained` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `The tribunal` DOES `disclose to every party the evidence and information obtained under section 21(5)` AT 3
#TRACE `s 21(6) the tribunal's duty to disclose the evidence it obtained` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `The tribunal` DOES `make notes of the proceedings` AT 3
#TRACE `s 21(8)(a) the tribunal's duty to make a summary of the facts and issues in dispute` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `The tribunal` DOES `make a summary of the facts and issues in dispute, as determined by the tribunal` AT 2
#TRACE `s 21(8)(b) the tribunal's duty to make notes of the proceedings` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `The tribunal` DOES `make notes of the proceedings` AT 2

§ `Tests -- s 22`

-- s 22(1): args = the claim is within the tribunal's jurisdiction, the order
#ASSERT `s 22(1) the tribunal may make the order` (JUST TRUE) `An order requiring a party to pay money to another party` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 22(1) the tribunal may make the order` (JUST TRUE) `An order dismissing the whole or any part of the claim` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 22(1) the tribunal may make the order` (JUST TRUE) `An order requiring a party to pay costs to another party` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 22(1) the tribunal may make the order` (JUST TRUE) `An order requiring an employer to reinstate an employee in the employee's former employment` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 22(1) the tribunal may make the order` (JUST TRUE) `Another kind of order` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 22(1) the tribunal may make the order` (JUST FALSE) `An order requiring a party to pay money to another party` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 22(1) the tribunal may make the order` NOTHING `An order requiring a party to pay money to another party` EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 22(2)
#ASSERT `s 22(2) the tribunal may take the matter into account in deciding whether to make a costs order` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 22(2) the tribunal may take the matter into account in deciding whether to make a costs order` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 22(2) the tribunal may take the matter into account in deciding whether to make a costs order` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 22(2) the tribunal may take the matter into account in deciding whether to make a costs order` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 22(3) the order is subject to any conditions the tribunal thinks fit to impose` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 22(4), (5)
#ASSERT `s 22(4) the total ordered to be paid for contractual and statutory disputes is within the claim limit` 20000 (JUST 20000) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 22(4) the total ordered to be paid for contractual and statutory disputes is within the claim limit` 20001 (JUST 20000) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 22(4) the total ordered to be paid for contractual and statutory disputes is within the claim limit` 20000 NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 22(5) the total ordered to be paid for wrongful dismissal disputes is within the claim limit` 20000 (JUST 20000) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 22(5) the total ordered to be paid for wrongful dismissal disputes is within the claim limit` 20001 (JUST 20000) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 22(5) the total ordered to be paid for wrongful dismissal disputes is within the claim limit` 20000 NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 22(6)
#ASSERT `s 22(6)(a) the amount of money ordered under subsection (1)(a), which does not include costs` 1300 300 EQUALS 1000  -- a total of 1300 with 300 costs: 1000 is the (1)(a) amount
#ASSERT `s 22(6)(a) the amount of money ordered under subsection (1)(a), which does not include costs` 500 0 EQUALS 500  -- no costs
#ASSERT `s 22(6)(b) the part of the payment applied to the amount under subsection (1)(a)` 500 1000 EQUALS 500  -- all of a small payment goes to the amount
#ASSERT `s 22(6)(b) the part of the payment applied to the amount under subsection (1)(a)` 1000 1000 EQUALS 1000
#ASSERT `s 22(6)(b) the part of the payment applied to the amount under subsection (1)(a)` 1200 1000 EQUALS 1000
#ASSERT `s 22(6)(b) the part of the payment applied to the costs under subsection (1)(c)` 500 1000 300 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 22(6)(b) the part of the payment applied to the costs under subsection (1)(c)` 1000 1000 300 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 22(6)(b) the part of the payment applied to the costs under subsection (1)(c)` 1100 1000 300 EQUALS 100
#ASSERT `s 22(6)(b) the part of the payment applied to the costs under subsection (1)(c)` 1300 1000 300 EQUALS 300
#ASSERT `s 22(6)(b) the part of the payment applied to the costs under subsection (1)(c)` 1500 1000 300 EQUALS 300  -- an overpayment is not applied to either
-- s 22(7)
#ASSERT `s 22(7) the claim or the part must be dismissed for lack of jurisdiction` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 22(7) the claim or the part must be dismissed for lack of jurisdiction` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 22(8), (9)
#ASSERT `s 22(8) the kind of mediation the tribunal may refer the dispute to` `From a mediation under Part 2 of a specified employment dispute` TRUE EQUALS JUST `Mediation under Part 2`
#ASSERT `s 22(8) the kind of mediation the tribunal may refer the dispute to` `From a mediation under Part 2 of a specified employment dispute` FALSE EQUALS JUST `Mediation under Part 2`  -- with or without consent
#ASSERT `s 22(8) the kind of mediation the tribunal may refer the dispute to` `From a tripartite mediation conducted by an approved mediator` TRUE EQUALS JUST `Tripartite mediation to be conducted by an approved mediator`
#ASSERT `s 22(8) the kind of mediation the tribunal may refer the dispute to` `From a tripartite mediation conducted by an approved mediator` FALSE EQUALS JUST `Tripartite mediation to be conducted by an approved mediator`
#ASSERT `s 22(8) the kind of mediation the tribunal may refer the dispute to` `From neither of those` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 22(9) the tribunal may order the parties to attend the mediation personally` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 22(9) the tribunal may order the parties to attend the mediation personally` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 22(10): 14 days after the order is made; counted over a month end
#ASSERT `s 22(10) the last day on which the tribunal may make the correction` (Date 25 2 2026) EQUALS Date 11 3 2026
#ASSERT `s 22(10) the last day on which the tribunal may make the correction` (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS Date 15 1 2026
#ASSERT `s 22(10) the last day on which the tribunal may make the correction` (Date 25 12 2026) EQUALS Date 8 1 2027
#ASSERT `s 22(10) the tribunal may make the correction` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 15 1 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE  -- the 14th day
#ASSERT `s 22(10) the tribunal may make the correction` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 16 1 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- the 15th day
#ASSERT `s 22(10) the tribunal may make the correction` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 22(10) the tribunal may make the correction` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 10 1 2026) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING  -- not one of the four things
-- Trace 8: correction on day 14 -> FULFILLED.  Trace 9: correction on day 15 -> also FULFILLED, read on the run: a MAY has no breach branch, so the trace cannot tell a late correction from an early one (finding in NOTES.md); the 14 days are carried by the two `s 22(10)` decision functions asserted above.
#TRACE `s 22(10) the tribunal's permission to correct an order within 14 days` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `The tribunal` DOES `correct an order made by the tribunal` AT 14
#TRACE `s 22(10) the tribunal's permission to correct an order within 14 days` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `The tribunal` DOES `correct an order made by the tribunal` AT 15
#ASSERT `s 22(11) the tribunal may make the correction on its own initiative or on the application of a party` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 22(12) the order may be enforced in the same manner as a judgment given or an order made by a District Court` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 22(12) the order may be enforced in the same manner as a judgment given or an order made by a District Court` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- the rulings of 2026-11-05 and the review's findings`

-- s 22(10), ruled I(a): "within 14 days after the date" is a period in the text's own words, so a correction outside it is JUST FALSE.  args = the date the order is made or the statement is issued, the date of the correction, the correction rectifies one of the four things
#ASSERT `s 22(10) the tribunal may make the correction` (Date 1 6 2025) (Date 16 6 2025) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- an order made on 1 June 2025, corrected on the 15th day
#ASSERT `s 22(10) the tribunal may make the correction` (Date 10 6 2025) (Date 25 6 2025) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- a statement of grounds issued on 10 June 2025, corrected on the 15th day
#ASSERT `s 22(10) the tribunal may make the correction` (Date 10 6 2025) (Date 24 6 2025) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE  -- the 14th day
#ASSERT `s 22(10) the tribunal may make the correction` (Date 1 6 2025) (Date 20 6 2025) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- late and not one of the four things: the period is tested first
-- s 22(4) and (5): "(if any)" -- a total of nothing cannot exceed a limit whatever the limit is (fork F11)
#ASSERT `s 22(4) the total ordered to be paid for contractual and statutory disputes is within the claim limit` 0 NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 22(5) the total ordered to be paid for wrongful dismissal disputes is within the claim limit` 0 NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
